---
layout: article
title: Manage organizations
description: Create and update Appwrite organizations from your partner platform using the Console Organization API.
---

Use the Organization API to provision and configure organizations as part of your onboarding flow.

# Create an organization {% #create-an-organization %}

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
import { Client, Organizations } from 'node-appwrite';

const client = new Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://cloud.appwrite.io/v1')
    .setProject('console')
    .setKey(process.env.APPWRITE_ORG_API_KEY);

const organizations = new Organizations(client);

const org = await organizations.create({
    organizationId: 'unique()',
    name: 'Acme Platform Customer',
    billingEmail: 'billing@example.com',
});
```
{% /multicode %}

Store the returned organization ID in your platform database and associate it with the customer record.

# Update organization settings {% #update-organization-settings %}

Update name, billing email, and preferences when customers change settings in your product:

{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
await organizations.update({
    organizationId: orgId,
    name: 'Updated name',
});
```
{% /multicode %}

# Map organizations to customers {% #map-organizations-to-customers %}

Maintain a stable mapping between your customer ID and Appwrite `organizationId`. Use this mapping for all Console API calls and audit logs.

